Telling a newbie to genocide rothes is counterproductive.  Rothes are a
valuable source of food in that particular stage of the early game, as
long as you know how to fight them.  Telling her how to *fight* or
*evade* rothes effectively is far more useful (and will also stand her
in good stead throughout the game; the essential tactical lessons
involved remain applicable).

Now, telling him to genocide soldier ants or plains centaurs or Uruk-hai
for similar reasons, that's sensible.
